text = "\"Frontier Texas!\" is a self-paced and self-guided museum experience.

After paying for your tickets at the front desk, you will begin in the Welcome Theater. If no one else is waiting to enter the museum, then our staff will begin the show for you when you are ready. Otherwise, the Welcome Theater runs every 12 minutes. The Welcome Theater's show is narrated by Buck Taylor, the \"Trail Guide\" for our museum. He will get you familiar with what you will see in the museum. After the show is done, you may then enter the museum.

There is a second theater near the end of the museum called \"The Frontier Experience\". This show is 20 minutes long, and will put you in the middle of various scenes such as a saloon shootout, a thunderstorm, and a buffalo herd stampede. This experience does have strobe lights and very loud audio sequences. We advise anyone sensitive to epilepdic seizures to skip this optional part of the museum. You may also leave this theater at any time by pushing on the exit doors.

When you are finished with the museum, you may exit through our Guns of the West display, and come back into our Gift Shop and Lobby."

